From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Chiou <chiouss@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 16:47:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: ath11k: advertise HT/VHT on 5 GHz for 5/6 GHz
 radios

When a QCN9074 reports a frequency range covering both 5 GHz and 6 GHz,
as it does with the board data of the Zyxel NWA220AX-6E where a single
radio serves both bands, ath11k registers both bands on one wiphy but
only sets up the HT/VHT capabilities of the 5 GHz band for single pdev
devices. hostapd then refuses to start a HT/VHT/HE AP on 5 GHz:

  Driver does not support configured HT capability [HT40*]

Add a patch that sets up the 5 GHz HT/VHT capabilities whenever the
5 GHz band has been registered. 6 GHz-only radios do not register 5 GHz
channels and keep their current behaviour.

Tested on the Zyxel NWA220AX-6E: 5 GHz up to HE80 and 6 GHz up to HE160
work on the same radio without firmware crashes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Mark Chiou <chiouss@gmail.com>
---
 ...ise-HT-VHT-on-5GHz-for-5-6GHz-radios.patch | 36 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/952-wifi-ath11k-advertise-HT-VHT-on-5GHz-for-5-6GHz-radios.patch

diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/952-wifi-ath11k-advertise-HT-VHT-on-5GHz-for-5-6GHz-radios.patch b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/952-wifi-ath11k-advertise-HT-VHT-on-5GHz-for-5-6GHz-radios.patch
